title = Emerald Cockroach Wasp
description = The emerald cockroach wasp, jewel wasp, or emerald jewel wasp (Ampulex compressa) is a solitary wasp of the family Ampulicidae. It is known for its unusual reproductive behavior, which involves leading a cockroach into a dug burrow and using it as a host for its larvae. It thus belongs to the entomophagous parasites.
